  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_006 (RNA-only, scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer) at 0.653 acc. RNA clearly dominates (0.485–0.653) over image-only resnet50 (0.208). The scvi_n200 encoder with multiprofile is the strongest RNA pipeline, and transformer≈avgpool for it. The only untested image encoder is imagenet_vit_l, which is substantially larger and likely more informative than resnet50. Question: Can adding a strong image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) to the best RNA pipeline (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer) via concat fusion beat the RNA-only ceiling of 0.653? Why this is the best use of experiment 8: With only 2 experiments remaining, we need to directly test whether multimodal fusion can improve on the current best. Resnet50-based multimodal is unlikely to help given its 0.208 image-only score, so imagenet_vit_l is the only viable image path. This configuration isolates the multimodal question using the already-validated best RNA settings, and if it succeeds we secure a new best; if it fails, the remaining experiment can test weighted fusion or confirm RNA-only as optimal."
